  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "image": "none",
  "questionText": "Let $f(x) = x^3 - 12x$. Find the stationary points of $f$ and determine their nature.",
  "solution": "$f'(x) = 3x^2 - 12 = 3(x^2 - 4)$, so stationary points occur at $x = \\pm 2$. $f''(x) = 6x$: at $x = 2$, $f''(2) = 12 > 0$, a local minimum with $f(2) = -16$; at $x = -2$, $f''(-2) = -12 < 0$, a local maximum with $f(-2) = 16$.",
  "tags": [
